From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kettle Linux <kettlelinux@kettlelinux.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:35:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: a resolution change's last buffer is not an
 error

When the firmware reports a resolution change, it returns an empty
capture buffer flagged PSC_LAST, which the driver passes on as
V4L2_BUF_FLAG_LAST. An empty buffer returned while streaming is also
flagged as an error unless it is a drain's last buffer, so the
resolution change's last buffer went to userspace with both LAST and
ERROR set.

That happens for the first sequence too when the client starts both
queues before the first frame, which Valve's arm64 Steam Remote Play
client does. It took the ERROR flag as a failed frame and restarted
the decoder at every frame. Exempt PSC_LAST as well.

Link: https://github.com/kettlelinux/kettlelinux/blob/2b7661b4d937d7efbb487c4bba84f8705be7cc5d/kernel/patches/40-kettle/1370-media-iris-a-resolution-change-last-buffer-is-not-an-error.patch
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_response.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_response.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_response.c
index f0782c4b1e6e..a76f597b4478 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_response.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_response.c
@@ -391,7 +391,7 @@ static int iris_hfi_gen2_handle_output_buffer(struct iris_inst *inst,
 	buf->flags = iris_hfi_gen2_get_driver_buffer_flags(inst, hfi_buffer->flags);
 
 	if (!buf->data_size && inst->state == IRIS_INST_STREAMING &&
-	    !(hfi_buffer->flags & HFI_BUF_FW_FLAG_LAST)) {
+	    !(hfi_buffer->flags & (HFI_BUF_FW_FLAG_LAST | HFI_BUF_FW_FLAG_PSC_LAST))) {
 		buf->flags |= V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR;
 	}
 
